<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows at $11.5 mln April 18.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows at $11.5 mln April 18.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $11.5 million surplus on April 18 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data suplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the Central Bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON APRIL 18</p>
<p>Exports: $263.5 million</p>
<p>Imports: $255.4 million</p>
<p>Finanancial buy: $254.8 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $251.4 million</p>
<p>Net surplus: $11.5 million</p>
<p>ARPIL DOLLAR FLOWS UP DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $2.958 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $3.146 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $3.995 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $3.490 billion</p>
<p>Net surplus: $317 million</p>
<p>NOTE: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>((--Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroon, 55 11 2485418))</p>
